WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.270
There's something really in me,
who likes to take this risk.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.730
And often, sometimes I think,
why the f*** did I do that?

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.080
I'm going to teach you
many different recipes,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.330
presentations, how to really
make something happen.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.520
I had a stepfather,
he was not a nice guy.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.910
I always wanted to leave.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.540
I was 14 years old
and I found a job.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.000
I said, "it's perfect,
I can leave the house."

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.980
You're going to learn how
to be a better cook at home.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.410
Teach your palate
little step by step.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.780
You can toast your peppercorns
in the oven to release the oil.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.650
Keep the pan.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.090
Don't rinse the pan.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.310
This is where we're
going to make our sauce.

00:00:50.032 --> 00:00:51.615
I was the chef at a
French restaurant.

00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:54.670
A manager comes to me and
says, "here is the new menu."

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.920
"What do you mean the new menu?"

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.045
"You didn't even talk to me."

00:00:57.045 --> 00:01:00.090
I got so pissed off at him,
I took off my apron and said,

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.840
"well then you f***ing
cook the menu."

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.550
I said, you know, I want to be
in charge of my own destiny.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.460
Instead of using parsley, I'm
going to use the carrot tops.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.050
Most people would
just throw it away.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.110
Don't use the
expensive olive oil

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.150
because it's a waste of money.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.970
If you want to start your day
with a Bloody Mary like that,

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.950
you don't going to stop.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.240
If you have passion
for what you do,

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.442
you're going to be
successful at the end.

00:01:27.442 --> 00:01:29.400
They're going to say,
"where did you learn that?"

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.320
Did you learn it at
the MasterClass,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.970
or did you go to
Paris for a year?

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:39.520
I'm Wolfgang Puck, and
this is my MasterClass.

